            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The edit correctly incorporates the governing statutory exception in paragraph (d)(5) (which provides that nothing in the section allows an individual access to information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding) into the reading of the access requirement under paragraph (d)(1). The resulting summary is accurate, complete, and faithful to the source text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal introduces an inaccurate requirement by stating that the agency must require every individual, whether accompanied or unaccompanied, to furnish written authorization before access. In fact, paragraph (d)(1) provides that the agency may require a written statement authorizing discussion specifically in the accompanying person's presence.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F010\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged draft C0000 omits the governing statutory limitation set out in paragraph (d)(5), which explicitly restricts access under this section for information compiled in reasonable anticipation of a civil action or proceeding. Because the unchanged statement lacks this governing exception, it is not an independently complete reading.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
